	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/html" rect="(180.0000000000001, -1230.6547619047624, 473.3333333333336, 54.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">&lt;div style="text-align:center;"&gt;
  &lt;div style="height:4px; background:blue; margin-bottom:8px;"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;span style="display:inline-block; background-color:blue; color:white; padding:10px 24px 10px 32px; font-size:28px; font-weight:bold;"&gt;
    Student Habits Classification
  &lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;div style="height:4px; background:blue; margin-top:8px;"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/markdown" rect="(117.08333333333326, -1072.5000000000002, 624.5833333333333, 677.5)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">## 1. Workflow for the “Exploration/Validation” Phase

**Widgets** (from left to right):

### `File`
- Load `train.csv`.
- Check that `lifestyle_profile` is correctly recognized as the **Target**.

### `Select Columns` *(optional but useful for teaching)*
- Make sure that `student_id` is set as **Meta** (and not **Feature**).
- Set **Features** as all the other columns except the target.

### `Data Table`
- Use it to display a few rows and explain the variable types.

### `Test &amp; Score`
- Connect the output of `Select Columns` to the input of `Test &amp; Score`.
- Choose several learners:
  - `Tree` (Decision Tree)
  - `kNN`
  - `Logistic Regression`
  - `Random Forest` or `Naive Bayes`
- Configure cross-validation, for example with `k = 5`.
- Display **Accuracy** and, if needed, **F1 score**.

### `Confusion Matrix`
- Connect the output of `Test &amp; Score`.
- Identify the most frequently confused classes and explain the errors.
</text>
		<text id="2" type="text/markdown" rect="(112.08333333333314, -109.46428571428572, 742.9166666666665, 829.5)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">
## 2. Workflow for Generating Predictions on the Test Set

To align with the competition logic using separate train and test sets:

### `File (train)`
- Use a `File` widget loaded with `train.csv`.

### `File (test)`
- Use a second `File` widget loaded with `test.csv`.

### `Select Columns` on the training data
- Configure it as before.

### `Classification Tree` *(or another selected learner)*
- Use the learner you want to train.

### Training
- Training is implemented through the connection between `Select Columns` and the learner.

### `Predictions`
Connect:
- the trained learner to the **learner** input of the `Predictions` widget,
- the output of `File (test)` to the **data** input of `Predictions`.

This generates predictions on the test set.

### `Data Table` *(connected to `Predictions`)*
- Visualize the predictions: a `prediction` column will appear.

### `Save Data`
- Save the result as a CSV file, for example `submission_orange.csv`.

For Kaggle submission, explain that the columns must be renamed to match the required format: `student_id,lifestyle_profile`, depending on the name Orange gives to the prediction column.</text>
